# Supabase Rules

## Client Configuration
- Always validate environment variables before creating client
- Use proper TypeScript types for database schema
- Implement proper error handling for database operations

```typescript
// ✅ Good Supabase client setup
const supabaseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
const supabaseAnonKey = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY

if (!supabaseUrl || !supabaseAnonKey) {
  throw new Error('Missing Supabase environment variables')
}

export const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey)
```

## Authentication
- Always check authentication status before protected operations
- Use proper session management
- Implement proper logout cleanup
- Handle authentication errors gracefully

## Database Operations
- Use Row Level Security (RLS) policies
- Implement proper error handling for all database operations
- Use transactions for related operations
- Validate data before database operations

## Security
- Never expose sensitive data in client-side code
- Use server-side operations for sensitive data
- Implement proper authorization checks
- Use environment variables for all secrets